---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const structuredData = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.url },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Method", item: `${site.url}/about/` }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Chaos Front Guide Method | Verification Policy"
  description="How Chaos Front Guide verifies gameplay notes, records sources, and decides what is ready to publish or index."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  image={site.shareImage}
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-header">
        <p class="system-label">EDITORIAL METHOD</p>
        <h1>Evidence before doctrine</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Chaos Front Guide is an independent, English-first reference site for one game. We publish
          observed results instead of generic game-catalog copy or unsupported build lists.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-grid">
        <section class="article-copy">
          <p class="system-label">01 / BUILD CONTEXT</p>
          <h2>Every claim names its conditions</h2>
          <p>
            A guide must identify the tested game build and verification date. When a result depends
            on a mission branch, squad setup, difficulty setting, or Demo limitation, the page states it.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="article-copy">
          <p class="system-label">02 / REPRODUCTION</p>
          <h2>Readers need a route back to the result</h2>
          <p>
            Published recommendations include repeatable steps, original captures, or another direct
            record of the condition. A community report can suggest a test, but cannot confirm it alone.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="article-copy">
          <p class="system-label">03 / FAILURE PATH</p>
          <h2>Useful advice includes its limits</h2>
          <p>
            Each guide records known risks, counterexamples, and a practical alternative when one is
            available. That is more useful than a universal "best build" claim.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="article-copy">
          <p class="system-label">04 / INDEXING</p>
          <h2>Only finished pages enter Google’s index</h2>
          <p>
            Release information based on official sources can be indexed now. Strategy routes stay out
            of the sitemap until the evidence above is complete, avoiding thin pages and stale claims.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
